# Lt. Arex, Ever-Adapting ({5}{G}{U}): "When Lt. Arex enters, draw three cards. You may put up to three land cards from
# your hand onto the battlefield tapped." (CR 121.1, 608.2c, 608.2d, 305.2). One land is already on the battlefield when
# it enters, so its characteristic-defining P/T (CR 604.3) is at least 1/1 and it is not a 0/0 put into its owner's
# graveyard by a state-based action (CR 704.5f) before this ability resolves. Four land cards are in hand when it
# resolves - three just drawn and one kept from an earlier turn - so the "up to three" is the limit: exactly three are
# put tapped and the fourth stays in hand. Putting them is not a land play (CR 305.2). Bot2's land cards in hand are
# not offered - only the controller's own hand is.

